R CMD config: answered by rzig, without make or sh

src/scripts/config evaluates etc/Makeconf and the site's and user's
Makevars through make (on Windows also through sh: rcmdfn.c starts
bin/config.sh with `sh`), so the query pkgbuild, pak and configure
scripts run first needed the build-tools group, although `rzig build`
compiles most packages without it. rzig's config mode
(zigbuild/tools/rzig/config.zig) reads the same files in the same order
with its make evaluator and prints what the script printed, with the
same options, messages and exit codes. A Makevars construct only make can
evaluate (`$(shell)` in `:=`, `define`, `!=`) ends it with exit 2 and the
file and line. R CMD dispatches to it on every OS: bin/Rcmd's case on
unix (R_HOME/bin/toolchain/rzig config ...), rcmdfn.c on Windows
(R_HOME/bin/toolchain/rzig.exe config ...). bin/config and bin/config.sh
are no longer installed. This replaces the earlier patch that only put
rzig's build-tools check in front of the script.
feat-config-rzig PLAN.md.

--- a/src/scripts/Rcmd.in
+++ b/src/scripts/Rcmd.in
@@ -52,6 +52,12 @@
     cmd="${R_HOME}/bin/Rdconv"
     extra="-t txt"
     ;;
+## r-zig: rzig answers R CMD config from Makeconf and the Makevars files,
+## without make (feat-config-rzig PLAN.md); bin/config is not installed
+  config)
+    cmd="${R_HOME}/bin/toolchain/rzig"
+    extra="config"
+    ;;
 ## removed in 2.15.0
   Rd2dvi)
     echo "R CMD Rd2dvi is defunct: use Rd2pdf instead"
